"paranoid.legal.title" = "Paranoid mode — full notice";
"paranoid.legal.body" = "Paranoid mode destroys data you configured, then shuts down the Mac.\n\n• Configured folders/files are deleted with rm -rf (best effort; not a secure overwrite guarantee on APFS).\n• Optional dedicated APFS volumes may be erased. Never the boot / Macintosh HD volume.\n• A local FileVault recovery-key backup file may be deleted if you configured one.\n• Lock, logout, and hygiene actions run in parallel with the wipe; hard shutdown follows the wipe time budget.\n• There is no grace period. A false trigger cannot be cancelled after the cable is pulled.\n• Unsaved work will be lost. Irreversible data loss is expected.\n• Do not use this on an employer or shared Mac unless you are explicitly authorized. You are solely responsible.\n• APFS TRIM and snapshots may retain remnants; this is not a forensic wipe.\n\nYou act at your own risk. This is not legal advice.";
